v1.3.16 (2026-08-16)
--------------------
Fix: usernames containing a space broke the entire hub user list. New:
password generator in the Create User dialog.

Fix — user list / edit broken by non-filesystem-safe usernames:
- _cert_path() validates hub/username against a filesystem-safe charset
  ([a-zA-Z0-9_.-]) before building a .p12 path — correct for cert file I/O,
  but SoftEther usernames are free-form (e.g. "Staale Kolbeinsen" has a
  space). list_users() and get_user() called _cert_path() directly for
  every user just to check has_p12, so one such username threw a 400 that
  took down the whole hub's user list, and made that user's own Edit
  modal fail outright
- Added _cert_path_or_none(): same validation, but returns None instead of
  raising. A name outside the safe charset is treated as "no p12 on disk"
  (correct — cert generation goes through the same charset check, so one
  was never written for that user anyway)
- Frontend: openEditUser() now wraps its data fetch in try/catch and shows
  the error in the modal instead of silently doing nothing; loadUsers()
  catches fetch failures and renders an error row instead of leaving the
  table showing stale data

New — password generator (Create User → Password auth):
- Length slider (6–64, default 16), and toggle switches for numbers and
  symbols, matching the existing toggle-switch style used elsewhere
- Generates via crypto.getRandomValues (not Math.random), fills both
  Password and Confirm Password, and switches those fields to visible
  text so the generated value can be read/copied
- Reopening the Create User modal resets the generator to defaults and
  re-masks the password fields
